1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,593
This guide installs Research and Engineering Router for Codex on Windows. Your main model

2
00:00:03,593 --> 00:00:06,000
stays in charge. The skill is free, while provider API charges may apply.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,161
Start in your project folder. You need Node for the Skills installer, and Python

4
00:00:11,161 --> 00:00:14,323
three point ten or newer for the helpers. The helper runtime needs no third

5
00:00:14,323 --> 00:00:15,000
party Python packages.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:26,059
Choose Local for this project only. This is the actual local installation, with output

7
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:28,000
shortened for readability.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,364
Choose Global for all projects under your user account. Add --global or -g. You

9
00:00:36,364 --> 00:00:40,000
do not need to run both installation commands.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Open the folder matching your installation scope. Use the project path for Local, or

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
your user profile path for Global.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,818
Jev is optional. Choose a provider profile with a matching endpoint, model and protocol.

13
00:00:57,818 --> 00:01:01,636
This demonstration uses an existing GapGPT profile. Other profiles are documented, but are not

14
00:01:01,636 --> 00:01:03,000
live tested in this video.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
New users create a private configuration outside the skill folder. These are setup instructions,

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
not commands executed during this recording. Keep an existing working configuration. For another provider,

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
copy its profile and replace placeholder settings.

18
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,818
On Windows, configure prompts for the provider key without echoing it, and stores encrypted

19
00:01:25,818 --> 00:01:29,636
credentials outside the skill. Secret input is not recorded here. Headless hosts can inject

20
00:01:29,636 --> 00:01:31,000
the configured environment variable instead.

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,148
Status confirms the selected route and credential availability without sending a model request. These

22
00:01:37,148 --> 00:01:41,000
are selected fields from the real run. Credential ready does not prove connectivity.

23
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,667
Dry run checks the request without sending it. The real output says sent false.

24
00:01:47,667 --> 00:01:51,000
This step is useful before a potentially billable connection test.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,162
Remove dry run to make the live call. Our real request succeeded on the

26
00:01:57,162 --> 00:02:01,324
first attempt and returned a refund score of zero point nine nine. This verifies

27
00:02:01,324 --> 00:02:04,000
the connection, not token savings. Provider charges may apply.

28
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,421
Now mention the skill in Codex and describe your real task. Reload the agent

29
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:14,842
if necessary. This is an example prompt, not a recorded coding result. The skill

30
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:18,000
screens large evidence sets and skips routing for small tasks.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,733
Earlier matched comparisons recorded thirteen point nine six percent fewer main model tokens for

32
00:02:23,733 --> 00:02:27,467
code audit, and six point four one percent fewer for research. Overall task time

33
00:02:27,467 --> 00:02:31,200
increased twenty point four two percent. These were two authored tasks, not a guarantee

34
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,000
for every workload.

35
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,625
The repository has provider setup, examples and the full recorded results. Try a real

36
00:02:36,625 --> 00:02:39,250
task and share feedback. If the skill helps your work, consider giving it a

37
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:40,000
GitHub star. Thank you.
